OL,24,ANext Page BLondon NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,372,370,120,260,000,100
PN,37103
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F371A1786969104
OL,3,CMet Police increased use of stop and
OL,4,Csearch by a fifth over last year
OL,6,FResearch released earlier this year
OL,7,Fsuggested black people are up to 48
OL,8,Ftimes more likely than white people to
OL,9,Fbe stopped and searched by police in
OL,10,Fwealthier parts of London.
OL,12,FAnalysis of every stop carried out by
OL,13,FMet officers in 2023, covering 152,000
OL,14,Frecords, also showed the grounds given
OL,15,Ffor search were more vague for black
OL,16,Fpeople.
OL,1,W h7}h7}j7}h7}h7}                 G3/8
OL,2,W+,"-'*%/*-'"-'*%/T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BLondon NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,372,370,120,260,000,100
PN,37104
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F371A1786969104
OL,3,CMet Police increased use of stop and
OL,4,Csearch by a fifth over last year
OL,6,FResearchers from Kings College London
OL,7,Ffound the three London ward areas with
OL,8,Fthe highest disproportionality were
OL,9,FEast Sheen in Richmond, where black
OL,10,Fpeople were 48 times more likely to be
OL,11,Fsearched than white, Dulwich Village,
OL,12,Fwhere the rate was 40 times, and
OL,13,FHampstead Town, where the figure was
OL,14,F38 times.
OL,16,FIn February, black Londoners were 3.4
OL,17,Ftimes more likely than white Londoners
OL,18,Foverall to be stopped and searched by
OL,19,Fpolice. The national rate is four
OL,20,Ftimes.
OL,1,W h7}h7}j7}h7}h7}                 G4/8
OL,2,W+,"-'*%/*-'"-'*%/T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
